14. Can a Java record be used as a REST controller response?

→ Yes, records are suitable for immutable response DTOs.
→ They automatically provide a constructor, accessors, equals(), hashCode(), and toString().
→ Spring Boot can serialize records to JSON using Jackson versions with record support.
→ Records are useful for transferring data without writing boilerplate getters and constructors.

Example:

public record StudentResponse(Long id, String name) {}

