28. What is the Strategy Design Pattern?

→ Strategy defines multiple interchangeable behaviours behind a common interface.
→ Each behaviour is implemented in a separate class.
→ The application selects the required implementation at runtime.
→ It avoids large if-else blocks when behaviour varies by type.

Example:

interface Report {
    void generate();
}

class PDFReport implements Report {
    public void generate() {
        System.out.println("Generating PDF");
    }
}

class ExcelReport implements Report {
    public void generate() {
        System.out.println("Generating Excel");
    }
}

